nss_core: size the command skb for the message, not the payload_len

nss_core_send_cmd() allocates the command skb with buf_size and then
copies size bytes into it:

	memcpy(skb_put(nbuf, buf_size), (void *)ncm, size);

The existing checks bound the firmware-supplied message length against
size and buf_size against PAGE_SIZE, but never size against buf_size,
so a caller passing a message larger than the payload size overruns the
skb data area into skb_shared_info. nss_wifili_tx_msg() is that caller:
sizeof(struct nss_wifili_msg) is 2096 while NSS_NBUF_PAYLOAD_SIZE is
1984, and the memcpy writes 112 bytes past the end of the skb buffer.

Size the allocation for max(size, buf_size) and let the existing
PAGE_SIZE bound cover that value. skb_put() keeps nbuf->len - and
therefore the payload_len the firmware sees - at buf_size; the message
bytes beyond it land in the skb tailroom instead of skb_shared_info.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>

--- a/nss_core.c
+++ b/nss_core.c
@@ -3386,13 +3386,16 @@ int32_t nss_core_send_cmd(struct nss_ctx
 		return NSS_TX_FAILURE_TOO_LARGE;
 	}
 
-	if (buf_size > PAGE_SIZE) {
+	if (max(size, buf_size) > PAGE_SIZE) {
 		nss_warning("%px: interface: %d type: %d tx request size too large: %u",
-					nss_ctx, ncm->interface, ncm->type, buf_size);
+					nss_ctx, ncm->interface, ncm->type, max(size, buf_size));
 		return NSS_TX_FAILURE_BAD_PARAM;
 	}
 
-	nbuf = dev_alloc_skb(buf_size);
+	/*
+	 * skb_put() below keeps nbuf->len, the firmware-visible length, at buf_size.
+	 */
+	nbuf = dev_alloc_skb(max(size, buf_size));
 	if (unlikely(!nbuf)) {
 		NSS_PKT_STATS_INC(&nss_ctx->nss_top->stats_drv[NSS_DRV_STATS_NBUF_ALLOC_FAILS]);
 		nss_warning("%px: interface: %d type: %d msg dropped as command allocation failed", nss_ctx, ncm->interface, ncm->type);
